  "sweeps": {
    "rule": "For every witness variable v of the honest assignment, add delta to z[v] (increment: delta = 1; flip: delta = 1 - 2 z[v], only where z[v] is 0 or 1) and re-decide every fixed row that contains v. 'undetected' counts variables for which no row becomes violated. 'zeroMultiplierOnly' counts undetected variables that appear only in B of rows whose A z is 0 (or only in A of rows whose B z is 0). 'unused' counts witness variables in no row.",
    "derivation": "Source reading of gadgets.rs, blake2b.rs, abi2.rs, lower.rs and circuit.rs: every allocated witness enters a row linearly (bit sums, XOR outputs, sum recompositions, limb equalities, products) except eq_uint's inverse, which appears only as `d * inv = 1 - f`. When d = 0 (equal operands) inv is free and affects no output. Equal-operand eq_uint sites: partial 1 (ensures liability_amount(invoice) == opening - amount); allocate 3 (requires units == quotient * 3 + remainder; ensures rounds == 0; ensures liability_amount(allocation_reserve) == remainder). quotient not = 0 has d = 7, so its inverse is determined.",
    "invoice/partial": {"increment": {"undetected": 1, "zeroMultiplierOnly": 1, "unused": 0}, "flip": {"undetected": 1, "zeroMultiplierOnly": 1, "unused": 0}},
    "reserve/allocate": {"increment": {"undetected": 3, "zeroMultiplierOnly": 3, "unused": 0}, "flip": {"undetected": 3, "zeroMultiplierOnly": 3, "unused": 0}},
    "limit": "A single-variable sweep finds free and unused witnesses. It does not prove witness uniqueness, which also needs every multi-variable compensation excluded; that remains a source argument (range-proven limbs, booleanized bits, functional XOR and sum rows)."
  }
}
